{'start': datetime.time(0, 0), 'end': datetime.time(0, 0, 31), 'text': 'A model is only as fair as the data and choices behind it. Today we look at where bias in machine learning actually comes from.'}
{'start': datetime.time(0, 0, 31), 'end': datetime.time(0, 1, 8), 'text': 'Bias usually enters through training data: if a hiring dataset reflects decades of skewed decisions, a model trained on it will faithfully reproduce that skew.'}
{'start': datetime.time(0, 1, 8), 'end': datetime.time(0, 1, 43), 'text': 'A landmark study found commercial facial recognition systems misclassified darker-skinned women at dramatically higher rates than lighter-skinned men - a direct consequence of unrepresentative training sets.'}
{'start': datetime.time(0, 1, 43), 'end': datetime.time(0, 2, 23), 'text': 'Fairness can be measured: demographic parity asks whether positive outcomes are distributed equally across groups, while equalized odds asks whether error rates are equal. The two often cannot be satisfied at once.'}
{'start': datetime.time(0, 2, 23), 'end': datetime.time(0, 2, 57), 'text': 'Documentation helps: datasheets for datasets and model cards force teams to state what data was used, what it covers, and where the model should not be applied.'}
{'start': datetime.time(0, 2, 57), 'end': datetime.time(0, 3, 33), 'text': 'Regulation is arriving - the EU AI Act classifies systems by risk and puts hard obligations on high-risk uses like hiring and credit scoring.'}
{'start': datetime.time(0, 3, 33), 'end': datetime.time(0, 4, 6), 'text': 'Our practical checklist: audit your data before training, measure error rates per subgroup, document limitations, and keep a human in the loop for consequential decisions.'}

