{'id': 62, 'start': datetime.time(0, 0), 'end': datetime.time(0, 0, 30), 'text': "You don't need a datacenter to specialize a large language model. This video is about fine-tuning on a budget."}
{'id': 63, 'start': datetime.time(0, 0, 30), 'end': datetime.time(0, 1, 6), 'text': 'Full fine-tuning updates every weight of the model and needs the memory to match - for a 70B model that means multiple high-end GPUs before you train a single step.'}
{'id': 64, 'start': datetime.time(0, 1, 6), 'end': datetime.time(0, 1, 47), 'text': 'LoRA - low-rank adaptation - freezes the base model and trains only tiny low-rank adapter matrices inserted into each layer. You typically touch well under one percent of the parameters and can merge the adapter back in afterwards.'}
{'id': 65, 'start': datetime.time(0, 1, 47), 'end': datetime.time(0, 2, 24), 'text': 'QLoRA goes further: quantize the frozen base model to four bits, then train LoRA adapters on top. A single consumer GPU can fine-tune a model that would otherwise need a cluster.'}
{'id': 66, 'start': datetime.time(0, 2, 24), 'end': datetime.time(0, 2, 59), 'text': 'Data beats scale here: a few thousand clean, well-formatted, task-specific examples routinely outperform millions of noisy scraped ones.'}
